IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ks-s55`
IMPORT `ks-types`
IMPORT `ks-membership`

-- KiwiSaver Act 2006 — GOAL 2: CONTRIBUTIONS.
--
--   "At what rate must the employer deduct from this pay, and how much; what
--    compulsory employer contribution is due; and the rules for rate
--    reductions, savings suspensions and non-deduction notices."
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2006_40.txt — Part 3,
-- ss 60-114.

§ `Goal 2 — contributions`

§§ `The contribution rate and the deduction (ss 62, 64, 66)`

-- s 64(1) "(a) 3.5% ... if section 60(1)(a), (b) or (c) first applied ... on or
-- after 1 April 2009 and the employee has not given ... a notice under
-- subsection (2) ...; (ab) 4% ... if section 60(1)(a), (b) or (c) first
-- applied ... before 1 April 2009 ...; (b) 8% ... if the employee gives ... a
-- notice requiring contributions to be deducted at that rate; or (c) 3% ...
-- if the payment of salary or wages is calculated on or after 1 April 2026
-- and the employee has a rate reduction under subpart 3B." (2) "the employee
-- may choose a contribution rate of 3.5%, 4%, 6%, 8%, or 10%". A notice
-- naming any other rate is not a notice under (2), so the default applies;
-- (a)(ii) the s 66A transitional rule and (a)(iii) a 2% rate chosen before
-- April 2013 give 3.5% (changed after the independent pass).
@ref s 64(1)-(2)
@export The contribution rate for an employee's pay under s 64 of the KiwiSaver Act 2006 (NZ), as a percentage of gross salary or wages: 3% with a rate reduction (pay calculated on or after 1 April 2026); otherwise the rate the employee chose (3.5, 4, 6, 8 or 10); otherwise 3.5%, or 4% where deductions first applied before 1 April 2009. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Contribution facts`  @desc When deductions first applied, any rate chosen by notice, whether there is a rate reduction, any savings suspension or non-deduction notice, the date the pay was calculated, and the gross salary or wages
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the contribution rate for` c MEANS
    IF   c's `has a rate reduction` AND c's `payment calculated on` AT LEAST Date 1 4 2026
    THEN 3
    ELSE CONSIDER c's `rate chosen by notice`
         WHEN JUST r THEN
            IF   r EQUALS 3.5 OR r EQUALS 4 OR r EQUALS 6 OR r EQUALS 8 OR r EQUALS 10
            THEN r
            ELSE byHistory
         WHEN NOTHING THEN byHistory
    WHERE
        byHistory MEANS
            CONSIDER c's `rate history`
            WHEN `deductions first applied on or after 1 April 2009` THEN 3.5
            WHEN `deductions first applied before 1 April 2009`      THEN 4
            WHEN `the s 66A transitional rule applied immediately before 1 April 2009` THEN 3.5
            WHEN `on a 2% rate chosen before the first pay period starting on or after 1 April 2013` THEN 3.5


-- s 66 "The employer must make deductions of contributions from each payment
-- of the employee's gross salary or wages of an amount equal to the
-- contribution rate." s 62(b), (bb): not while on a savings suspension or
-- with a valid non-deduction notice.
@ref ss 62, 66
@export The KiwiSaver deduction from a payment of salary or wages under ss 62-66 of the KiwiSaver Act 2006 (NZ): the contribution rate times the gross salary or wages, or nothing during a savings suspension or while a non-deduction notice is valid. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Contribution facts`  @desc The facts that fix the rate, any suspension or non-deduction notice, and the gross salary or wages of the payment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction from the pay` c MEANS
    IF   c's `on a savings suspension or with a non-deduction notice`
    THEN 0
    ELSE c's `gross salary or wages for the pay` TIMES `the contribution rate for` c DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 64(4) "An employee may not change his or her contribution rate in
-- relation to an employer at intervals that are less than 92 days apart
-- unless the employer agrees." The same 92 days for rate reductions (s
-- 101S(2)), savings suspensions (s 108) and non-deduction notices (s 112B(3)).
@ref ss 64(4), 101S(2), 108, 112B(3)
GIVEN last IS A DATE, next IS A DATE, agrees IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the change is at least 92 days after the last, last` last `, next` next `, employer agrees:` agrees IF
    agrees OR Day next MINUS Day last AT LEAST 92

§§ `Compulsory employer contributions (ss 101C-101FC)`

-- s 101C "the employee— (a) is paid salary or wages from which the employer
-- deducts or is required to deduct an amount ...; and (b) is aged 16 or over;
-- and (c) is not entitled to withdraw an amount ... under clause 4 ...; and
-- (ca) must not have made a withdrawal under clause 12B ...; and (d) is not a
-- defined benefit scheme member."
@ref s 101C
GIVEN e IS AN `Employer contribution facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee meets s 101C` e IF
        e's `deductions are made or required from the pay`
    AND e's `employee aged` AT LEAST 16
    AND NOT e's `may withdraw under clause 4 (lock-in ended)`
    AND NOT e's `made a congenital condition withdrawal under clause 12B`
    AND NOT e's `a defined benefit scheme member`

-- s 101D(4) "CEC rate is— (a) 3% if the employee has been granted a rate
-- reduction under subpart 3B ... and ... the employer chooses to apply this
-- rate; or (b) 3.5%."
@ref s 101D(4)
GIVEN c IS A `Contribution facts`, e IS AN `Employer contribution facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the CEC rate for` c `and` e MEANS
    IF c's `has a rate reduction` AND e's `the employer applies 3% for a rate reduction` THEN 3 ELSE 3.5

-- s 101D(1) "The amount of a compulsory employer contribution is a positive
-- amount calculated using the following formula" — symbols lost in the
-- conversion; read as (payment of gross salary or wages × CEC rate) − other
-- contributions − hybrid schemes amount, the items in the order (3)-(6)
-- define them (BRIEF.md). s 101FB: none in a grace period; s 101FC: none
-- where other contributions or the hybrid amount reach the CEC rate (which
-- the formula already gives).
@ref ss 101A, 101C, 101D, 101FB, 101FC
@export The compulsory employer contribution for a payment of salary or wages under ss 101A-101FC of the KiwiSaver Act 2006 (NZ): for an employee who meets s 101C (deductions made, aged 16 or over, not past the withdrawal age, no congenital condition withdrawal, not a defined benefit member), the gross salary or wages times the CEC rate (3.5%, or 3% for a rate reduction if the employer chooses), less the employer's other contributions and any hybrid schemes amount, never below 0; nothing in a grace period. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Contribution facts`  @desc The gross salary or wages of the payment and whether the employee has a rate reduction
      e IS AN `Employer contribution facts`  @desc The s 101C facts, the employer's choice of the 3% rate, other contributions and the hybrid schemes amount for the period, and whether a s 101FB grace period applies
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compulsory employer contribution for` c `and` e MEANS
    IF   `the employee meets s 101C` e AND NOT e's `in a grace period with no deductions`
    THEN max 0 ((c's `gross salary or wages for the pay` TIMES `the CEC rate for` c `and` e DIVIDED BY 100)
                MINUS (e's `other contributions for the period` PLUS e's `hybrid schemes amount for the period`))
    ELSE 0

-- s 101F(2) to a complying superannuation fund "no later than 1 month after
-- the payment of salary or wages".
@ref s 101F(2)
GIVEN paid IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to pay a complying fund, salary paid` paid MEANS
    `the last day under s 55 for a deadline of` (`add months` paid 1)

§§ `Rate reductions (ss 101L-101S)`

-- s 101L(3) "the period for which the rate reduction is required must be no
-- less than 92 days and no more than 1 year." s 101M "The Commissioner must
-- grant a rate reduction ... if the application is made in accordance with
-- section 101L." FORK F6: the ending date is the last day of the reduction
-- (s 101N "the date on which the rate reduction will end"), so both days
-- count (changed after the independent pass).
@ref ss 101L, 101M
GIVEN starts IS A DATE, ends IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a rate reduction must be granted, starting` starts `, ending` ends IF
        Day ends MINUS Day starts PLUS 1 AT LEAST 92
    AND ends LESS THAN `add years` starts 1

§§ `Savings suspensions (ss 102-112B)`

-- s 102 "(a) at any time after the Commissioner receives the first
-- contribution ..., if the person is suffering, or likely to suffer,
-- financial hardship; or (b) at any time after 12 months have expired since
-- the earlier of" the first contribution to the Commissioner or a provider,
-- or first membership of a complying fund.
@ref s 102
GIVEN first IS A DATE, applied IS A DATE, hardship IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for a savings suspension, first contribution` first `, applying` applied `, in financial hardship:` hardship IF
        (hardship AND applied GREATER THAN first)
    OR  applied GREATER THAN `add months` first 12

-- s 104 "(2) A savings suspension granted in respect of an application made
-- under section 102(a) must be granted for a period of 92 days, unless the
-- Commissioner agrees to a longer period. (3) ... under section 102(b) ...
-- (a) a minimum period of 92 days; and (b) a maximum period of whichever is
-- the shorter of— (i) 1 year; or (ii) the period specified in the
-- application." FORK F2: 1 year as 365 days.
@ref s 104
GIVEN hardship IS A BOOLEAN, asked IS A NUMBER, `longer agreed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days of savings suspension granted, hardship:` hardship `, days asked` asked `, longer period the Commissioner agrees` `longer agreed` MEANS
    IF   hardship
    THEN max 92 `longer agreed`
    ELSE max 92 (min 365 asked)
